//? Title: Beam Search

\toc

> Mathematics and algorithm

Beam search expands one depth layer, ranks candidates by heuristic \(h\), and
retains only the best \(B\).  It bounds memory by \(O(Bd)\) but may discard the
only solution and is therefore incomplete.

```
beam <- {start path}
repeat: expand all beam paths; return a goal if found
sort children by h(endpoint); retain first B
```

> C\+\+ example

```{cpp, results="output", exports="both", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <datamunge/algorithms/search_batch.hpp>
#include <iostream>
int main(){auto r=datamunge::algorithms::beam_search(3,{{0,1},{1,2}},0,2,{2,1,0},1);std::cout<<r.found;}
```
